title: 'pallet-revive: measure the contract's own account in host function benchmarks'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `CallSetup` no longer whitelists the executing contract's `System::Account`, so its accesses
    are now part of the weights of `seal_call_transfer`, `seal_instantiate`,
    `seal_instantiate_transfer`, `evm_instantiate`, `evm_instantiate_transfer`, `seal_balance`,
    `seal_terminate` and `seal_terminate_logic`. Runtimes with their own `pallet_revive` weights
    have to re-run the benchmarks. So do precompile benchmarks built with
    `pallet_revive::precompiles::run::CallSetup` that access the calling contract's account.
    A benchmark that relied on the whitelist in `CallSetup::new` or `CallSetup::default` now has
    to whitelist the account explicitly.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    A call with value, creating a contract, `SELFBALANCE` and `SELFDESTRUCT` now also pay for the
    contract's own account: one read, a write where the balance or the nonce changes, and its
    proof size. Previously, a nested contract called without value did not pay for it.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
